The driver provides support for the following Archive and Wangtek
boards:  Raw  devices  are  indicated  by an preceding the device
name.  The driver can be opened with either rewind on close or no
rewind on close options.  The tape format is specified by  adding
8  or 16 to the device number.  For example, for the wt0 device’s
raw rewind on close device nodes, is the 150  MByte  density  de‐
vice,  is  the  120 MByte density device, and is the 60 MByte de‐
vice.  The driver conflicts unpleasantly  with  the  driver  (SMC
adapters)  at  the  same I/O address.  The probe reprograms their
EEPROMs.
